# Drafted by Gemini (R14 poet), edited.

~ quill_start
Narrator: An ink-stained pilgrim taps a silver nib against his chin, utterly deaf to the howling wind and the smell of cold ash.
pilgrim_quill [smile]: Hush now, don't trample the meter. I am composing a masterwork for Father Renathyr, to be declaimed at the next Night of Flames.
* Let us hear this ode of yours. -> quill_ode
* [if flag.quill_asked] Help with the ode -> quill_help
* Are you related to Ambrose Quill in Wickermoor? -> quill_cousin
* Leave him to his verses. -> END

~ quill_ode
pilgrim_quill [smile]: "O Crimson Father, high in your grand monastery, burn all the wicked in your holy fire-blastery!" Notice how "blastery" captures the sheer percussive theology of the pyre.
Narrator: He beams at you, waiting for the applause that surely follows a freshly minted noun.
quest pilgrims_bad_poetry asked
set quill_asked
-> quill_start

~ quill_cousin
pilgrim_quill [angry]: My cousin Ambrose is a provincial hack who counts syllables on his knuckles. I have never read a single line of his, and I know for a fact they are dreadful.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Blastery, darling? Even a headless jester wouldn't rhyme that for the cheap seats.
-> quill_start

~ quill_help
pilgrim_quill [neutral]: You wish to offer notes on my stanza? Speak quickly, then, before the muse hardens like tallow.
* [Performance DC 12] Recite a better rhyme for him -> quill_fixed | quill_flat
* [Persuasion DC 12] Tell him not to recite it -> quill_withheld | quill_flat
* Offer a plain rhyme: "dread" with "bed" -> quill_fixed
* [ends:pilgrims_bad_poetry] Let him recite it as it is. -> quill_recites

~ quill_flat
pilgrim_quill [sly]: He sniffs, tilting his chin toward the red glass above. No, no, your cadence is all muddled; explain yourself properly if you mean to meddle.
-> quill_help

~ quill_fixed
pilgrim_quill [weary]: A pedestrian couplet, I suppose, though it spares the priors a coined word. Take this fair copy for your trouble, and I shall use the tamer verse.
Narrator: The poem is only slightly less lethal to the ear, though it may now spare the poet's neck.
set quill_outcome = "fixed"
quest pilgrims_bad_poetry done
give quill_ode
-> quill_start

~ quill_withheld
pilgrim_quill [sad]: Pearls before hounds, you say? Perhaps you are right; these mountain priors have the ear of a quarryman, so I shall keep the parchment in my coat.
set quill_outcome = "withheld"
quest pilgrims_bad_poetry done
-> quill_start

~ quill_recites
approve delphine_ravelle +2 silas_vane +2 tobin_hayward -1: You encouraged the poet to declaim his disastrous rhyme aloud
pilgrim_quill [smile]: Wise of you not to tamper with perfection. When the torches touch the kindling, my voice shall ring from the bell tower to the valley floor!
Narrator: When the verse is later read aloud, the courtyard answers without a single clap, and by morning the poet wears a purpled eye and a strangely lighter heart.
set quill_outcome = "recited"
quest pilgrims_bad_poetry burned
-> END
